# Golden files are byte-exact fixtures, so their line endings are part of the
# assertion and must survive checkout unchanged.
#
# Without this, the eol attribute is unspecified and translation depends on each
# checkout's `core.autocrlf`: a developer set to `input` sees LF and a Windows CI
# runner set to `true` sees CRLF, so `pkg/metrics`' exposition-format conformance
# test (ADR-0050) passed locally and failed only on the windows-2022 cell.
#
# `text eol=lf` rather than `-text`: the file stays text as far as Git is
# concerned, so it still diffs readably when the fixture legitimately changes,
# but it is always written out with LF.
*.golden text eol=lf
